      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Blast-radius (approximation)\n\nThis view is a **BGP-adjacency-based** approximation: it lists switch/peer sessions where `spx_bgp_neighbor_up == 0`. If a spine or a leaf<->spine link is down, the affected leaf adjacencies appear here.\n\nTopology (rail-optimized, 2 planes):\n- **PL1**: spine `F41-34`, leaves `F38-29` / `F42-48`\n- **PL2**: spine `F41-32`, leaves `F38-35` / `F38-27`\n- All 4 DGX nodes connect to every leaf.\n\n_Follow-on:_ full per-DGX-rail blast-radius would map the `topology.dot` edges (dgx<->leaf, leaf<->spine) onto downed sessions.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Blast Radius Notes",
      "type": "text"
